; --- The legacy tripwire ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
; MEASURED, not inferred. Two of the six callback prefixes page a strain-of-day carousel whose
; only data source is a table that migration 083 dropped. The reader is src/db/mod.rs:1041; its
; one caller is src/bot/callbacks.rs:387, which writes unwrap_or_default() and so turns the query
; error into an empty vector. An empty vector makes the index lookup at :388 miss, the arm sends
; nothing, and the surface is alive precisely because it fails quietly.
; tests/retired_table_wiring.rs:66-76 (:66-75 until 2026-09-26) already carries this as one of four declared survivors and
; states in its own words that retiring the carousel is a product decision rather than a
; consequence of the drop. That ruling belongs to REUSES_LEGACY_RETIREMENT_ID. This file records
; only that the wire is still attached, and one thing that file will want:
; THE CAROUSEL HAS NO ENTRANCE. A grep of all of src/ for the two prefixes finds them produced at
; exactly two places, src/bot/callbacks.rs:406 and :412 -- both inside the handler for those same
; prefixes. No command, no menu and no notification renders the first page, so the only way to
; press a button is to have pressed one already. The surface is not merely empty; it is
; unreachable, and the retirement owner can weigh a removal against zero live entry points.
pub const LEGACY_PREFIX_COUNT : u8 = 2;
