; MARKED COPY, NOT AN ORIGINAL. The next two counts are turbobaby/legacy-retirement's: it is the
; retirement owner, it declares them as DROPPED_TABLE_COUNT and ALLOWLIST_SIZE, and it is the
; file a reader should change first. They are repeated here because the tripwire paragraph above
; is unreadable without them, and a copy that is not marked as one is how two files start
; disagreeing in silence. The owner's values are pinned beside them and an invariant holds the
; pair equal, so a divergence fails the gate here instead of being discovered by a reader.
; Both were re-read at SOURCE on 2026-09-21, not taken on trust from the owner: migration 083
; carries 6 DROP TABLE statements (:82-84 and :88-90) and tests/retired_table_wiring.rs holds 4
; Survivor entries (:49-82; :49-83 since 2026-09-26). Owner and source agree, which is what makes the copy safe to keep.
