; RETIRED 2026-09-25, and the tripwire above is now a record of what was wired, not a reading of
; what is. The owner ruled that day that nothing cannabis-related may appear anywhere (answer 12 of
; a numbered list; turbobaby/legacy-retirement records the ruling as OWNER_RULING_2026_09_25_AT and
; this file does not restate it). The two prefixes keep their own arms in route_callback, so a
; button already under an old message is still recognised rather than falling to Unknown, which
; answers the press and does nothing; a press now answers with the rental menu -- the one the menu
; command sends, built once by rental_menu in src/bot/commands.rs -- written over the old card when
; Telegram still lets the bot edit it and sent as a new message when it does not. That path reads
; no table. The reader LEGACY_READER names is still compiled: it is public (and the ignored test
; tests/integration_strain_of_day.rs called it until 2026-09-26, when it began to test the retirement
; instead), so its survivor entry stays and the allowlist size this file copies does not move. It has NO production caller any more:
; LEGACY_CALL_SITE, LEGACY_ERROR_IS_SWALLOWED and both LEGACY_BUTTON_PRODUCERS describe code that is
; gone and are kept as the 2026-09-21 reading they were. The Rust variant is now
; CallbackAction::RetiredCarouselPage and carries no page index; ACTION_STRAIN_OF_DAY_PAGE keeps its
; number and its name here, because a contract constant is never shown to anybody and every
; assertion that names it would move for nothing.
pub const CAROUSEL_RETIRED_AT : str = "2026-09-25";
