; --- The absence this file closes ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; Each PRIOR_ count is a grep over specs/ run on 2026-09-21 BEFORE this file existed, and a
; snapshot of a growing corpus is exactly the kind of number that rots into a lie. It rotted.
; The *_AFTER_THE_WAVE pair below was read while the wave was still landing, and both figures
; are now too small; they are KEPT as the readings they were and SUPERSEDED by the dated pair
; that follows, because deleting a measurement hides that the drift happened at all.
; RE-MEASURED 2026-09-21 against the finished 43-file corpus, excluding this file:
;   grep -ril telegram specs/          -> 22 of the other 42, not 12.
;   a slash-prefixed command name      -> 5 of the other 42, not 1.
; THE POINT SURVIVES BOTH, BUT NOT IN ITS OLD WORDS, so the old words are withdrawn. The claim
; used to be that every telegram hit is "a column name, an identity field or a D14 privacy
; field". That is NO LONGER TRUE and is not repaired by a bigger number: several of the new hits
; name Telegram as a PLATFORM rather than as a column -- the WebApp SDK and menu button in
; runtime_config, the host tab in webapp_bridge, the outage and the refusal in notification_queue,
; the exported type TelegramId in validation_bounds, the handle grammar in events_booking.
; What IS still true, and is the only thing this file ever needed, is narrower: none of the 22
; declares a BOT COMMAND SURFACE. The machine-checkable proxy for that is the trio below, all
; three re-run today and all three still 0 outside this file -- parse_mode, callback_data and
; BotCommands. Those are the absences this file closes.
; The five slash hits were opened one by one on 2026-09-21 and not one is a command roster:
; turbobaby/customer-surface names /menu as a CLIENT UI ROUTE (Route::Menu) and says in the same
; breath that no tab produces it; turbobaby/client-errors names /admin inside the HTTP route
; GET /admin/promo-report; turbobaby/referral-program names /start three times only to DISCLAIM
; the grammar, saying it owns no /start grammar; turbobaby/deeplink names /start as the link
; form of the payload it co-owns with this file; turbobaby/ai-assist names /joke and /fact while
; counting ask_grok call sites behind CALL_SITE_COUNT. Two of the five -- /menu and /admin --
; are an HTTP or UI path that merely SHARES A SPELLING with a bot command, which is the trap
; this whole paragraph exists to stop: a slash plus a word is not a command surface.
pub const PRIOR_SPECS_MATCHING_TELEGRAM : u8 = 6;
pub const PRIOR_SPECS_MATCHING_PARSE_MODE : u8 = 0;
pub const PRIOR_SPECS_MATCHING_CALLBACK_DATA : u8 = 0;
pub const PRIOR_SPECS_MATCHING_BOTCOMMANDS : u8 = 0;
pub const PRIOR_SPECS_NAMING_A_SLASH_COMMAND : u8 = 0;
; The two figures below were read MID-WAVE and are both superseded; see CORPUS_FILE_COUNT and
; the SPECS_*_2026_09_21 pair. They are kept because a withdrawn measurement is evidence and a
; deleted one is not. Their names say "after the wave"; the wave was not over when they were read.
pub const SPECS_MATCHING_TELEGRAM_AFTER_THE_WAVE : u8 = 12;
pub const SPECS_NAMING_A_SLASH_COMMAND_AFTER_THE_WAVE : u8 = 1;
pub const THE_AFTER_THE_WAVE_PAIR_WAS_READ_MID_WAVE : bool = true;
pub const THE_ONE_SLASH_COMMAND_HIT : str = "turbobaby/ai-assist, in the prose behind CALL_SITE_COUNT -- and no longer the only one; see SPECS_NAMING_A_SLASH_COMMAND_2026_09_21";
pub const SPECS_MATCHING_PARSE_MODE_AFTER_THE_WAVE : u8 = 0;
pub const SPECS_MATCHING_CALLBACK_DATA_AFTER_THE_WAVE : u8 = 0;
pub const THE_BRIEFS_TELEGRAM_ZERO_IS_REFUTED : bool = true;

; The dated re-measurement. Denominator named on purpose: a bare count over a corpus that grows
; is the defect being corrected here, not a fix for it.
pub const CORPUS_FILE_COUNT : u8 = 43;
pub const CORPUS_FILES_OTHER_THAN_THIS_ONE : u8 = 42;
pub const SPECS_MATCHING_TELEGRAM_2026_09_21 : u8 = 22;
pub const SPECS_NAMING_A_SLASH_COMMAND_2026_09_21 : u8 = 5;
pub const SPECS_MATCHING_PARSE_MODE_2026_09_21 : u8 = 0;
pub const SPECS_MATCHING_CALLBACK_DATA_2026_09_21 : u8 = 0;
pub const SPECS_MATCHING_BOTCOMMANDS_2026_09_21 : u8 = 0;
; Re-measured 2026-09-22 and deliberately NOT bound: a census of the corpus moves with every new
; contract. The 43 and 42 above are KEPT as the 2026-09-21 reading and the denominator of the
; 2026_09_21 counts. "The finished 43-file corpus" was not finished: 14b01ac added
; order_presentation.t27 and person_naming.t27 later on 2026-09-21, and specs/ holds 45 tracked
; .t27 files. Re-run at a33e500 over the 44 other files, the same five greps: telegram reaches 23,
; one more -- turbobaby/person-naming, which names Telegram as the platform whose updates deliver a
; customer's name, and a telegram id and handle among what it refuses to carry (D14's privacy
